An image takes a reference the way a link does: ![alt][r], and the collapsed
form ![alt][] uses its alt text as the label. The alt text may be empty: ![][r].

A cross-reference with auto text is </#section-id>, and #section-id on its own
is a tag.

The fifth braced spelling is {=highlighted=}, and it holds its own delimiter in
{=a=b=} the way the other four do.

[^n]: a footnote definition whose first word is prose, not a destination

[r]: /i.png
